  "faq1q": "How does XenDirekt work?",
  "faq1a": "Type the seller's MTN MoMo number and the amount in Rwandan francs. We show the name registered to that account, the fee and what your card will be charged. Tap Pay, confirm with Face ID or your PIN, and the seller receives francs in their MoMo account.",
  "faq2q": "Will I be charged if a payment fails?",
  "faq2a": "No. Your card is only held first and charged after the seller's MoMo account has received the money. If the seller can't receive it, the hold is released and you are not charged.",
  "faq3q": "Which numbers can I pay?",
  "faq3a": "Any active MTN MoMo account in Rwanda. Other networks are not supported yet.",
  "faq4q": "Is my card safe?",
  "faq4a": "Your card details are entered on our licensed payment partner's secure page. XenDirekt never sees or stores your card number or security code.",
  "faq5q": "What fees do I pay?",
  "faq5a": "You see the XenDirekt fee, the exchange rate and the exact total in your card's currency before you pay. Your bank may add its own foreign transaction fees.",
  "faq6q": "What is the extra check from my bank?",
  "faq6a": "Banks often ask you to confirm the first payment with a card (3-D Secure), for example with a code or in your banking app. It protects you from fraud.",
  "faq7q": "The seller says the money didn't arrive. What now?",
  "faq7a": "Open the payment in History and tap Report a problem. The payment reference is attached automatically and our team will look into it.",
  "faq8q": "Why is my payment being checked?",
  "faq8a": "Sometimes the mobile money network doesn't answer in time, or a payment needs a quick safety review. We'll update you within 30 minutes, and you'll never be charged twice.",
